; Match-arm pattern binders are ARM-SCOPED on every backend: a binder named
; after a builtin must not hijack calls to that builtin after the match.
; (Regression test: wasm codegen kept arm binders in its flat locals map,
; which routed the later [len "hello"] through a stale closure call and
; produced an untranslatable module.)
[type B [Full i64]]
[fn main []
  [match [Full 7]
    [Full len] [println len]
    _ [println 0]]
  [println [len "hello"]]
  [match 1
    0 [println 100]
    1 [println 200]
    other [println other]]
  [println [len "!"]]]
